<title>JAPAN: Comson says has difficulty raising funds for notes.</title>
<headline>Comson says has difficulty raising funds for notes.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese machinery maker Comson Corp said on Wednesday it is having trouble raising 100 million yen to cover promissory notes due on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Comson has 300 million yen worth of promissory notes due on Thursday, Comson president Toshimi Matsuda told a news conference in Osaka.</p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, Comson said it posted a parent current loss of 403 million yen in the six months to May 31, against a current profit of 74 million yen in the same period a year ago.</p>
</text>
